From chuck at sharpsteen.net  Sat Jan  7 23:26:20 2012
From: chuck at sharpsteen.net (Charlie Sharpsteen)
Date: Sat, 7 Jan 2012 14:26:20 -0800 (PST)
Subject: [Tikzdevice-bugs] Error when using raster image and reverting
 axis
In-Reply-To: <f6cb403e-8441-4069-a6da-0b04c28db3f9@d10g2000vbh.googlegroups.com>
References: <f6cb403e-8441-4069-a6da-0b04c28db3f9@d10g2000vbh.googlegroups.com>
Message-ID: <18548407.1210.1325975181121.JavaMail.geo-discussion-forums@prnp7>

I see a similar error on OS X. The problem is that when the axis is 
reversed, R passes a negative width to the C routines. Since the R 
documentation made no mention of this behavior, I wrote the raster routines 
for tikzDevice under the assumption that width and height were positive 
numbers.

Thanks for reporting, this has been logged as issue #53:

  https://github.com/Sharpie/RTikZDevice/issues/53

-Charlie

